      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I found most Panels and Inverters are manufactured by companies you have never heard of, so this made selection difficult. Given just about everything is now manufactured in China (usually to a good quality) I didn't find the companies who relied on made in Germany and made in Japan etc not helpful if its a company you don't know. Most Manufacturers warranties were the same. Some Installation companies advertised longer warranties but only on the the most expensive systems.It was important to me that the company also arranged connection to the Grid and installed the Meter. This part though is dependent on the Energy Company and is often quoted separately (or not quoted on at all) which makes the process a little stressful. The Panels & Inverter were installed a week ago as advised by RME when I ordered the system. They are awaiting release by Integral of the Meter that needs to be installed by the RME electrician.",
